      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "A number needs a counting word",
      "text": "After a number, Thai puts a counting word: สองอัน (two items). กี่ (\"how many\") takes the same slot: กี่อัน? The money word บาท counts itself: ห้าบาท.",
      "explains": [
        "th.counting-ki",
        "th.numbers"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "kind": "culture",
      "title": "ป้า, auntie",
      "text": "Thai people call an older woman ป้า (aunt) even when she is a stranger, and the name ป้าแดง means \"Auntie Daeng\". It is warm and respectful.",
      "explains": [
        "th.address-pa"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 0
    }
  ],
